ce:section.ce:para:
When it comes to organisms, the ER is an essential steroid receptor that is engaged in a wide variety of biological activities. It has been proved that ER can regulate the differentiation of preadipocytes and also has a role in the development of obesity (Santos et al., 2018). Molecular docking analysis demonstrated that BPF was able to bind to ERα through hydrophobic interactions and hydrogen bonds, suggesting its potential for interaction with the estrogen receptor (Ma et al., 2023). In accordance with the findings of our earlier research, BPF has the ability to induce ER, which in turn causes macrophages to produce inflammatory chemicals (Zhang et al., 2021). To confirm the involvement of ER in this process, the ER antagonist ICI 182780 was applied to test the hypothesis that ER regulates BPF's effects on 3T3-L1 preadipocyte differentiation. As shown in Fig. 5
                        A–C, co-treatment with ICI 182780 and BPF inhibited BPF's promotion of lipid droplet production and intracellular TG content in 3T3-L1 preadipocytes. Additionally, the role of ER in BPF's upregulation of differentiation-related genes and proteins was investigated. Consistent with the results for lipid droplet formation and TG content, the enhancing effect of BPF on PPARγ, C/EBPα, adiponectin, and FABP4 gene and protein expression was significantly reduced by the ER antagonist (Fig. 6
                        ). These results demonstrated that ER played a role in modulating BPF's effect on differentiation of 3T3-L1 preadipocytes.
